{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Why do you look at one another?</b> — Do not show yourselves satiated before the children of Esav and Yishma'el (Ta'anit 10a); at that hour they still had grain. And from others I heard that it is an expression of scarcity — why should you be diminished in the famine — and similar to it is 'and he who waters will also be watered' (ומרוה גם הוא יורה), according to Rashi's language (Rashi on Genesis 42:1). And the words of the others have no substance. And what they say — do not show yourselves satiated before the children of Yishma'el and the children of Esav — I do not understand, for the children of Yishma'el and the children of Esav are not now in the land of Canaan, and why should he not say that they should not show themselves satiated before the children of the land of Canaan? Perhaps the children of Yishma'el and the children of Esav were coming from their own land to Yosef to buy grain, and they would come by way of the land of Canaan passing through it, and he said to them that they should not show themselves satiated before them, lest they suspect that Yaakov has grain and come to him to eat bread with him in his house. And if so, what he said — 'and we shall live and not die' — is a different reason: he warned them to be careful with the little that is in their hands, and that they should go to purchase from it, so that they would not die when the bread that is in their hands runs out. But the correct interpretation of 'why do you look at one another' in this place is: you should have set out immediately when you heard that there is grain in Egypt, for they were already in danger if they did not hasten to the matter. And this is the reason for 'and we shall live and not die.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "In the line 'and he who waters will also be watered,' Ramban quotes Proverbs 11:25 to support reading תתראו as an expression of pouring/ watering; the Hebrew idiom is preserved as quoted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:27.584486536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}